{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q125177","formula":"Cu₄Cd(SO₄)₂(OH)₆·4H₂O","hill":"CdCu4H14O18S2","elements":["H","O","S","Cu","Cd"],"composition":{"H":14.0,"O":18.0,"S":2.0,"Cd":1.0,"Cu":4.0},"names":{"en":"Niedermayrite","uk":"Нідермайрит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Niedermayrite is a rare hydrated copper cadmium sulfate hydroxide mineral with formula: Cu4Cd(SO4)2(OH)6·4H2O. It crystallizes in the monoclinic system and occurs as encrustations and well formed vitreous blue-green prismatic crystals. It has a specific gravity of 3.36. Niedermayrite was named for Gerhard Niedermayr (born 1941), an Austrian mineralogist affiliated with the Naturhistorisches Museum in Vienna, Austria.","uk":"Нідермайрит — рідкісний гідратований мінерал, гідроксил-сульфат міді та кадмію з формулою: Cu 4 Cd ( SO 4 ) 2 ( OH ) 6 ⋅ 4 H 2 O {\\displaystyle {\\ce {Cu4Cd(SO4)2(OH)6*4H2O}}} . Кристалізується в моноклінній системі і зустрічається у вигляді наростків та добре сформованих склоподібних синьо-зелених призматичних кристалів. Має питому вагу 3,36."},"fame":9,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-1201664","atoms":91,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[5.612,0.0,0.0],[0.0,22.329,0.0],[-0.209,0.0,6.196]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":2.052,"y":5.582,"z":3.207,"el":"Cd"},{"x":3.351,"y":16.747,"z":2.989,"el":"Cd"},{"x":-0.154,"y":0.018,"z":4.64,"el":"Cu"},{"x":-0.154,"y":22.348,"z":4.64,"el":"Cu"},{"x":5.457,"y":0.018,"z":4.64,"el":"Cu"},{"x":5.457,"y":22.348,"z":4.64,"el":"Cu"},{"x":-0.052,"y":11.183,"z":1.556,"el":"Cu"},{"x":5.559,"y":11.183,"z":1.556,"el":"Cu"},{"x":-0.052,"y":0.0,"z":1.556,"el":"Cu"},{"x":-0.052,"y":22.329,"z":1.556,"el":"Cu"},{"x":5.559,"y":0.0,"z":1.556,"el":"Cu"},{"x":5.559,"y":22.329,"z":1.556,"el":"Cu